{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>If she is evil in her master's eyes.</b> Nevertheless, if she does not find favor in his eyes, he shall not marry her, lest he come to hate her. Rather, the father and the master shall endeavor to redeem her." "<b>To a foreign people he shall not have power, to sell her, in his betrayal of her.</b> The father, in betraying his daughter by selling her — as it says: הֲלוֹא נׇכְרִיּוֹת נֶחְשַׁבְנוּ לוֹ כִּי מְכָרָנוּ (Genesis 31:15). And this applies after the verse has shown the case of a foreign agent (פֹּעַל אִישׁ נׇכְרִי) in Israel — that an Israelite man has purchased an Israelite daughter not for the purpose of marriage — so he shall not have power to sell her thereafter to such a foreign people."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:39.857898580Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}